      "adjudicatedAt": "2026-09-05",
      "note": "The authored key stands and the blind answer is wrong on the committed evidence. The dataTable row \"a ruler\" holds \"The kingdom has a ruler\" under The Greek, \"ruled by a figure\" under The Norse, and an empty string under The Egyptian, so the Egyptian column is the one that gives nothing. The drawing says the same thing and says it more plainly than the JSON does: in fig-l2-three-realms.svg every row places its cells at x=78, 239, 400 and 561, and the \"a ruler\" row at y=342 carries text at 239 and 561 and NOTHING at 400, directly under the heading \"The Egyptian\" which itself sits at x=400. No cell shifted to fill the blank. The blind pass reads the dataTable JSON rather than the picture, and the likely error is an off-by-one across the leading row-label column \"three traditions\", which would align the heading The Greek with the Egyptian column data. A child sees the aligned drawing, not the JSON, so the ambiguity the blind pass is built to detect is not present. The item rebuts the blind answer in its own distractorRationale for that choice: \"The Greek column does fill that row in: it reads The kingdom has a ruler.\" The key and every rationale index were re-derived from text identity during the key-spread re-key and were re-checked here: the key carries no rationale and each distractor rationale matches its own choice text."
